  "facts": [
    "Opened September 3, 1959, Liberty Bridge instantly became Zagreb's central artery, linking Trnje with Novi Zagreb and replacing the older 1938 Sava Bridge that forced commuters to detour westward.",
    "Designed by Krunoslav Tonković, the bridge’s shallow arch spans 1,600 tons of steel and stone carved from Brač, a testament to mid‑century engineering ambition.",
    "Since 2019, a multi‑phase overhaul—valued at 27 million kuna—has upgraded footpaths, repaired rusted steel arches, and installed a new drainage system, aiming for full reopening in 2026."
